// C3.5 / ADR 0072 (negative): a call to an effecting fn inside a larger expression.
//
// `do_work() + 1` needs the perform's frame reified around the `+ 1`, which is the
// c35d embedded shape — but c35d only recognises a literal `perform`, so a CALL in the
// same position matched nothing.
//
// Before ADR 0072 this did not produce a diagnostic. It produced an INTERNAL COMPILER
// CRASH: `snc build` panicked inside inkwell with "Found PointerValue … but expected
// the IntValue variant", because the straight-line emitter asked for the `i64` the
// call's declared type promised and got the `Kont*` the ABI actually returns. A panic
// on a legal user program violates the project's own rule against `unwrap`/`panic!` on
// user-program input, which is why the refusal — not the crash — is the fixture.
//
// The `perform Io.read() + 1` spelling of this program compiles and runs, and always
// did. That contrast is the whole defect in one line.

effect Io {
    read() -> i64;
}

fn do_work() -> i64 ! { Io } {
    perform Io.read()
}

fn caller() -> i64 ! { Io } {
    do_work() + 1
}

fn main() -> i64 {
    handle caller() with {
        Io.read(k) => k(41)
    }
}
